  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "Two radioactive materials <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> have decay constants <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>25</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math> respectively. If initially they have the same number of nuclei, then the ratio of the number of nuclei of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> to that of A will be &quot;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>e</mi></math>&quot; after a time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math> is _____ .",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "9",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>According to radioactive decay formula,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>N</mi><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mi>&#955;</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math>, here,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></math>&nbsp;is the initial number of nuclei in a radioactive material.</p><p>Given here,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>25</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></math>.</p><p>And&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mi>e</mi></math></p><p>For radioactive material&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>For radioactive material&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>N</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p>Thus, the ratio&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>B</mi></msub><msub><mi>N</mi><mi>A</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></mfrac><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&#183;</mo><msup><mi>e</mi><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mn>1</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mrow><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi></mrow></msup></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mfenced><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfenced><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></math></p><p>Time,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>&#955;</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>25</mn><mi>&#955;</mi><mo>-</mo><mn>16</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>9</mn><mi>&#955;</mi></mrow></mfrac></math>.</p><p>Hence, the value of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>9</mn></math>.</p></blockquote>",
    "image": null
  },
